**Root Causes**
vlan5 SVI is Down (server02): In Cumulus Linux, an SVI (vlan5) will remain in a DOWN state unless at least one physical access port or trunk assigned to VLAN 5 is physically UP. If vlan5 is down, FRR considers 10.20.20.0/24 inactive and refuses to advertise it into BGP.

Quick Workaround (Force Advertisement)
If you want server02 to force-advertise 10.20.20.0/24 regardless of link state, create a dummy loopback route on server02:

**Solution 1**: Fix the Interface State (Recommended)
Assign a physical port to VLAN 5 and bring it up on server02 so vlan5 transitions to the UP state:

**Solution 2**: Add a Static Null/Blackhole Route
Add a static route on server02 so the kernel routing table contains 10.20.20.0/24, which satisfies the import check:
nv set vrf default router static 10.20.20.0/24 blackhole == DONOT WORK
nv set vrf default router static 10.20.20.0/24 via blackhole == DONOT WORK

**Solution 3** Correct Commands to Complete the Setup
Pointing the static to lo or set a blackhole/Null0 route
*Option A*: Pointing via lo: 
nv set vrf default router static 10.20.20.0/24 via lo
*Option B*: Standard Null0/Blackhole in NVUE: 
nv set vrf default router static 10.20.20.0/24 via Null0


*nv set vrf default router bgp address-family ipv4-unicast network 10.10.10.0/24* IGP
*nv set vrf default router bgp address-family ipv4-unicast redistribute static*   Incloplete



